#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-server-dns: Server mode's game download cache (LANCache) and ad blocker (AdGuard Home), 1.13
(docs/SERVER-MODE.md; mockups docs/mockups/next-update/server-cache.png and server-adblock.png).

Both are off until you turn them on, and both run on this PC as system containers (root Podman: they need ports 53
and 80) that are never part of starting the PC: no [Install] on their units; hearth-server-dns.timer (enabled only
while one of them is on) starts them a minute after the PC starts. A broken one only stops itself.

One DNS server for both: AdGuard Home answers your Hearth devices (on your home network and over Tailscale) and, if
your router hands it out, everything else on your Wi-Fi. With the ad blocker on it blocks ads and trackers; with the
cache on it sends the game stores' download names (Steam, Epic Games, Battle.net, Xbox / Microsoft Store: each with
its own switch) to LANCache on this PC, which keeps each download and gives it to every other device at home-network
speed. Your Hearth devices use it only while it answers (hearth-dns-client on each of them: back to normal lookups
within seconds when this PC can't be reached), so nothing ever waits for the server.

Run through pkexec by hearth-server-mode (49-hearth-memory.rules: the person at the device, no password prompt).

  hearth-server-dns status               JSON: settings, whether each runs, today's numbers (also without root:
                                         /run/hearth/server-dns/status.json, written by the watcher)
  hearth-server-dns cache on|off         the game download cache
  hearth-server-dns store STORE on|off   steam | epic | blizzard | xbox
  hearth-server-dns cache-place DIR GB   where the cache lives and how big it may get (the oldest games leave first)
  hearth-server-dns cache-empty SURE     empties it (SURE = "sure": the dashboard asks twice)
  hearth-server-dns ads on|off           the ad blocker
  hearth-server-dns ads-pause SECONDS    stop blocking for a while (0: block again now)
  hearth-server-dns allow DOMAIN         let a site that breaks through (from here or your phone)
  hearth-server-dns list ID on|off       Hearth Shield's block lists (main tv phone scam games adult; only main is on
                                         until you turn another on)
  hearth-server-dns block DOMAIN         always block a site (unblock DOMAIN: not any more; unallow DOMAIN likewise)
  hearth-server-dns safe-search on|off   family rules: search engines' and YouTube's safe search
  hearth-server-dns device NAME on|off|pause   one device (by its Tailscale name, or "lan" for everything else on
                                         your Wi-Fi): blocking on, off, or paused for an hour
  hearth-server-dns run-dns | run-cache  what hearth-server-dns.service / hearth-lancache.service run
  hearth-server-dns watch                what hearth-server-dns-watch.service runs: numbers every few seconds
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1. Settings: /etc/hearth/server-dns.json (atomic, a .bak,
an unreadable file is kept aside and never written over; only what you change is changed).
"""
